94359	Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.	<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Ghostweave Vest, along with information about delivery location and payment.  At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>
94360	Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.	<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Soul Pouch, along with information about delivery location and payment.  At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>
94369	Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.	Ansirem has told me much of the elemental lords and I am afraid that we have good reason to fear Al'Akir now that the wards that have hidden Zephras are down. If the Windlord chooses to attack us, we stand no chance to defend ourselves while we are here in his domain.\n\nHigh Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger we are in, and more importantly, what our intentions are for our mission to Azeroth. We will find the means to save our home. I swear it.
94373	Bring 2 Frostmane Bear Pendants to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.	Aye, the time's come, young shaman. Ye've grown stout and sturdy, like the stone beneath our boots. Takin' up the shaman's path shows ye've got the wisdom o' the mountain, even before ye've proven yerself.. Ye've the grit of stone to walk the earth's path.\n\nBut to earn its favor, ye must face it proper. South o' here, the Frostmane trolls live in a cave.\n\nBring me two of their necklaces they wear--crafted from the Iceclaw bears. Then we'll speak more of yer future.
94374	Find the Spirit Stone and drink the Earth Sapta.	Aye, sapta's a brew forged with magic, bindin' our spirit to the elements. Only a few shaman know the recipe, and it's nae for the weak-willed. Drink it, and ye will see what others can't. Hold true--it's only to be drunk in a sacred place.\n\nHead north to the Spirit Stone, tucked at the end of a hidden path up the mountain. Drink it there... see what the earth has to show ye.
94375	Bring the Rough Quartz to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.	Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Teo Hammerstorm as proof o' our meeting. He will craft a totem for ye, and this pebble will be the heart o' it. As small as it may seem, ye will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest o' things can outlast many others.\n\nBe patient, <Name>. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks o' ye. In the end, ye shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect ye.
94411	Slay 6 High Order Apprentices in Shen'dar Highlands.	Be warned, members of the High Order have been seen in the vicinity of the standing stones north of the village. We have warned them time and again to not meddle at our sacred sites, but they are growing more bold in pushing us. Prove your resolve to us by going to the standing stones and dispersing them.\n\nI am loathe to condone outright bloodshed, but do what you must to drive them off. Return to me when its done.
94413	Slay 6 Windshaper Novice Seers in Shen'dar Highlands.	The recent emergence of the ley lines on the surface of Zephras has been profound for our order. We have more direct and tangible access to the energies that permeate this place and it has increased our understanding of said magic greatly.\n\nThe Windshapers, however, view these emergences as scars on the land that must be "healed". This is an affront to our order and is something we simply cannot abide.\n\nGo to the ley line in the forest to the southwest and drive off the Windshapers you find there.
94414	Speak with Halaan Hawk-Eye and borrow his gift to view the anchor pylon in the distance.	Greetings, young <Name>. I often times come here to look upon the ancient anchor pylon. Gifts from the spirits of the winds, they bind and sustain our island. Of late however, their magic has grown unstable and inconsistent.\n\nThey suffer no distress I can see. Their splendor has not changed.\n\nIf you'd like, I can lend you my gift to look upon them yourself.
94427	Speak to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity.	A key tenant of being a paladin is the pursuit of divinity. This is not the pursuit of godhood, but merely the pursuit of good itself, for good's sake. We've all arrived at this place due to tragedy of one form or another, and it would be easy to lose that grace that defined us as paladins in life.\n\nGo to the Undercity and seek out Tanis Alderwood in the Trade Quarter. They are in need, and they could benefit greatly from some grace.
94434	Bring 10 Linen Cloth to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity.	Wait, you want to... help? Why would a paladin want to help a beggar like me?\n\nWell, I suppose that you could be of some assistance.\n\nIts my wife you see. She, well... she's falling apart. I mean that literally. The apothecaries can stitch her back together right as rain, but they are about the Dark Lady's business and none are available to help. If you could perhaps bring me some fresh cloth then I could at least make her a wrapping to hold her together while we wait for the apothecaries.
94435	Return to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep.	I don't know why you'd go out of your way to help me, but I appreciate it. If someone sent you my way, tell them I appreciate them too. You'll always have a friend in Tanis Alderwood, <class>.
94436	Speak with Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.\n\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement.	It's time to demonstrate your ability to channel one of the light's greatest gifts.\n\nThe item I just gave you is called the Symbol of Life. Take care, as it may cause you some discomfort to handle a talisman of the light such as this. The light may be anathema to the force that created us, but it is still our guide and ally. The pain reminds us of this.\n\nGo see Deathguard Billmuth downstairs. He just arrived and he has petitioned us for aid. Show him and the Forsaken what a true paladin can do.
94438	Take the Symbol of Life and use it to resurrect Deathguard Falgan at Venomweb Vale.\n\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement.	Falgan and I were sent on a mission to scout out scarlet activity in Venomweb Vale. We managed to sneak close enough to one of their camps to hear about new orders involving an attack on Brill. Before we could decide what to do next, I stepped on a twig and the noise alerted them to us.\n\nFalgan yelled at me to run, so I ran. By the time I realized he wasn't with me, I was halfway to Brill. That brave idiot probably stayed behind to hold them off for me.\n\nPlease, find my friend and help him if you can.
94440	Retrieve the Scarlet Crusade Attack Plans from the Scarlet Crusaders at Venomweb Vale, and return to Deathguard Billmuth at Tyr's Watch.	These Scarlet Crusaders often carry satchels with their deployment orders. We know an attack is coming, but if we can recover their orders, we can warn the rest of the Deathguard and prepare an ambush.\n\nYou are clearly an impressive paladin. Kill these scarlet animals and retrieve a copy of their orders and bring them back to Deathguard Billmuth. He'll take it from there.
94441	Speak with Danitha Morr in the keep at Tyr's Watch.	Please give my thanks to Danitha Morr and tell her that the rest of the Deathguard will hear about the service that the paladins of Tyr's Watch performed for us.\n\nYou have a lot of promise as a paladin, and I am proud to have those like you among the ranks of the Forsaken. Dark Lady watch over you, <name>.
94449	Find Bruegs Kindleborn in Dun Morogh.	It's been long since ye were last tested, <Name>. Ye've shown patience, aye -- but now it's time ye learned of chaos... of destruction. Fire's call is loud, and if ye're ready to pay its price, it'll speak to ye.\n\nSeek out Bruegs Kindleborn, far east in the mountains. He dwells in a cave above South Gate Outpost. He'll know if ye're truly ready.
94465	Bring the Torch of the Dormant Flame to Braldir Ashmantle in Loch Modan.	Aye, ye've the strength to bear the totem o' fire, lad--but strength alone won't make ye ready.\n\nBeyond the Valley o' Kings, in the crags of Loch Modan, lies a hidden path to one o' our sacred peaks. There, Braldir Ashmantle guards the Shrine o' the Dormant Flame.\n\nTake this torch to him--it shows yer intent. Return it burnin' by the shrine's brazier, and I'll see ye earn the totem proper.
94466	Bring 1 Fire Tar and 1 Reagent Pouch to Braldir Ashmantle in Loch Modan.	Bah, ye didn't trek all this way for tales, did ye, <name>? Ye seek the Eternal Flame and the fire totem.\n\nFirst, ye'll need a sapta to bind yer spirit to the flame.\n\nI'll craft it--but I'll need two things: fire tar from Tunnel Rat Geomancers in the kobold caves up north, and a reagent pouch from a Stonesplinter Seer lurkin' in the southern hills. Dangerous work, but worthy of the flame.
94467	Defeat the Minor Manifestation of Fire, and place the Glowing Ember in the brazier atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame.	The fire sapta's ready, <name>. Now ye face the flame. Use it at the shrine, then climb to the peak. There, ye'll see the spirit--he'll not strike 'til ye do, but he'll know ye see him.\n\nStrike fast, lad. The longer ye wait, the stronger he burns. When he falls, take his glowing embers and place 'em in the brazier. Light the torch and earn the fire's favor.
94468	Bring the Torch of Eternal Flame to Bruegs Kindleborn in Dun Morogh.	Torch firmly in hand, you turn away from the brazier and look out over Loch Modan. You feel an excitement tugging at your spirit as the wind picks up and forces the flame to dance violently.\n\nYou start off down the path back to Dun Morogh in search of Bruegs Kindleborn.
94472	Speak to Teo Hammerstorm for another Earth Sapta.
94484	Find and speak with Elegael Thornpaw in the northeastern part of Shadowgale Forest.	A moment, if you will <Name>. Are you headed towards Shadowgale Forest? There is a druid conclave there in a cave to the northeast. I have been waiting on word from them but their correspondence is long overdue.\n\nWith Ban'aethall in ruins and all the unrest lately I worry something dire may have happened. Please, if you are able go, seek out Elegael Thornpaw and put my mind at ease.
94485	Collect 8 Lady's Tear Moss.	If we are to save my fellows in the Nightclaw Den, I am going to need some ingredients for a poultice. The first and most important is a spindly moss called Lady's Tear. It typically grows on the base of the trees here in Shadowgale.\n\nThis moss secretes a sticky substance that acts as an antiseptic and is perfect for binding open wounds. I have gathered what little I can reach but I know there is more in this forest.\n\nGo and be swift. We are going to need a lot if the injured I left behind still live.
94486	Collect 20 feathers from the Shadowgale Shrieklings in Shadowgale Forest.	The other ingredient I need for the poultice is feathers from the Shadowgale shrieklings that roam this forest. In their juvenile form, the shrieklings have insulative feathers which would be ideal to put over the moss. These feathers will prevent the antiseptic sap from drying out and will provide at least some protection against the elements.\n\nBe warned, the shrieklings are normally docile but they have been incredibly hostile of late. Their large talons can easily disembowel you if you aren't careful.
94487	Collect 10 Bloodied Heirlooms from Al'Aketh Footsoldiers and Al'Aketh Stormchasers in the Shadowgale Forest.	The Al'aketh Cultists ambushed us with no warning, though their motives remain a mystery to me. I knew these cultists had clouds in-between their ears, but I never imagined they would upset the delicate balance here on Zephras with such brutality. Go, slay as many as you can and take their heirlooms if they wear any.\n\n<Elegael spits.>\n\nThese storm cursed cultists don't deserve to be called shen'dorei. The beasts of the forest can have their bodies. Their ashes don't deserve the winds.
94488	Kill Commander Haalien and bring his head to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.	The reason for cultists presence here still baffles me, but I smell a familiar scent over the bloodshed.\n\nOne of our circle druids, Haalien, disappeared months back. It appears he's thrown his sorry hide in with the cultists.\n\nShow him what happens when he spills the blood of his kin! Take his head and return it to me.
94489	Enter the Nightfang Den and heal 7 druids and find Jorel Windsinger in Shadowgale Forest.	I have finished the poultices. Quickly, take them to the druids in the cave, north just across the clearing. I know my brethren are in much more dire condition than I. They are likely too injured to heal their own wounds. There are so few of us shen'dorei druids that every life is precious.\n\nBefore you go, I have a selfish request. My mate, Jorel Windsinger was in dire condition when I left. Please, see to his wounds if he still lives.
94490	Bring the Ripped Missive to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.	<Tucked behind one of Haalien's bracers is a note that's been slightly torn and bloodstained in your fight. It looks like it contains useful information for about the cultist motivations for the attack on the druid den. Elegael would be interested in this intel.>
94491	Give the missive to Lotheluum in Valannar and tell him what has transpired.	It would appear that there is a correspondent hiding somewhere in Valanaar feeding information to the cult. I am clearly in no shape to make the journey, but Lotheluum needs to know what transpired here.\n\nHe should also know the fate of those who are no longer with us. Thanks to your help I think we can handle the rest of the situation from here, thought the damage has been done.\n\nPlease go swiftly, <Name>. I hope our paths will cross again someday. Until then, I have cultists to slay.
94493	Speak with Elegael Thornpaw in the northeastern part of Shadowgale Forest.	Thank goodness our message got to Lotheluum. Wait, where are the rest of the reinforcements? Surely it is not just you they sent?\n\n<Elegael pales as you explain yourself.>\n\nSo the message did not get to Valanaar. We are in dire straights indeed then.\n\n<Elegael sighs deeply then looks resolute.>\n\nThen we must handle this on our own. Time is of the essence.
94494	Find Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.	Long has it been since ye were last tested, <name>. Ye have shown patience thus far in yer studies, but the time has come for ye to learn about the purity of water.\n\nSeek out Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan. He is along the north western edge o' the lake, south of Stonewrought Dam. Ye  will find him there at his burrow hut. Good luck to ye, <name>.
94495	Find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.	If there's one truth ye need to learn about water, it's this: water means rebirth. It carves stone, cleanses filth, and heals the weary -- but only when it's pure. Taint it, and it'll ruin all it touches.\n\nIf ye seek the water sapta, find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands. Her family dwells in a cave beneath the southern falls.\n\nGo on then, don't let the river outrun ye.
94497	Fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the bottom of the waterfalls below Hervdana's cave and return it to her in the Wetlands.	Ah, so ye've come seekin' the sapta, have ye? Well then, listen close, love. To find understandin' and earn the sapta, ye must seek water in its various forms. As ye gather the samples, keep yer eyes open. Watch the beasts that guard it, the land it nourishes, and how it changes lives.\n\nWe'll start simple: fill this skin at the base o' the falls, where the fresh meets the brackish. Go on now, and mind the marsh.
94499	Fill the Empty Red Waterskin at Stonewatch Falls near the Nightcrawler Murlocs and return to Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.	Aye, Redridge drinks deep from Lake Everstill, but by the time the waters tumble down Stonewatch Falls, somethin' has seeped in. The murlocs down there are big, twisted brutes. Not like the ones ye find here or in the Loch. Lucky for the townsfolk they keep to the base o' the falls.\n\nBring a sampling to me. I've a mind to find out if it's magic, venom, or somethin' worse that's taintin' the waters near that old fort.
94500	Fill the Unfilled Blue Waterskin at the waters of Astranaar in Ashenvale and return to Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.	Take this waterskin and journey deep into the emerald shade o' Ashenvale. Astranaar rests cradled by waters untouched by corruption. Ruins litter the bed o' the lake, hinting at a bygone era. Bring back a sample from the lake. Pure, ancient, and possibly enchanted water.\n\nIt's the last liquid I need before I send ye back to Norric.\n\nBoard the boat in Menethil to Auberdine, it stops in Southshore on the way over.\n\nAnd mind yerself... the forest's got eyes, and they don't blink.
94501	Bring the Vial of Purest Water to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.	Norric will have one more task for ye before rewarding ye with the water totem rites. The vial of water I've given ye is necessary for whatever that task is. Go now and find him. We shall meet again some day.
94502	Cleanse the corruption at Stendel's Pond in Westfall.\nReturn to Norric in Loch Modan when finished.	In Westfall, outside o' Moonbrook lies Stendel's Pond. Once a pure spring, now touched by dark forces. The spirits there 'ave gone silent.\n\nYe must face the corruption that fouls the waters. Take its bracers and the last drops o' Hervdana's potion, then place 'em on the shrine. That'll call forth a spirit, cleansed and true. Speak with it, learn what ye can.\n\nBring me proof the deed's done, and I'll grant ye the totem.
94503	Speak to the Minor Manifestation of Water in Westfall.	Light erupts as the final word leaves your lips. The hiss of water turning to mist fades into silence, and your senses reel as the corrupt spirits around you unravel, their essence scattered like ash in the wind.
94505	Bring the Shard of Water to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.	Take shard. Take shard and give life.\n\nGive life and understand. Understand water is life... corruption stops life.\n\nYou protect and give life with water's power.
94559	Seek out the Al'Aketh Turncoat in the Shen'dar Highlands.	There is a turncoat amongst the Al'Aketh. They claim to know the cult's true intentions for the island and want to come in, but will only do so with assurances of protection.\n\nThis defector is hiding at a house just northwest of Valanaar, just inside the highlands. I need someone who can discreetly go there, find the traitor, find out and escort him back to us. This might be a trap, but if this information is as important as this traitor claims, its worth some risk.
94568	Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong and observe the conversation.	The turncoat clearly was afraid of the what the cult had planned, enough so to defect and seek our aid. It's truly unfortunate that he is dead and took his secrets to the grave with him.\n\nWe must discuss this further to determine our next steps.
94638	Find and kill Ur'endra in the Shen'dar Highlands.	You have come to me in hopes of learning to take a shape of strength. I have a task for you, though it lays heavy on my heart.\n\nMy mate, Ur'endra, has lost herself to madness and has begun to attack her own kin. Without the winds many creatures have begun to lose themselves, and with Ur'endra's great might she poses a dire threat to the delicate balance. She roams the Shen'dar Highlands to the northwest of here.\n\nShow me you have the fortitude to end her suffering and I shall grant you my blessing.
94774	Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.	You've caught the attention of our superiors, <name>. They've asked you travel to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Laurena. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.
94775	Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.	Elune bless you, good <race>. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.\n\nOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Cathedral of Light as soon as possible to speak with High Priestess Laurena. It seems you've done well to garner such attention. I wouldn't spend too much time here--your people have need of you.
94776	Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.	Time's come for you to head to Stormwind, <name>. High Priestess Laurena in the Cathedral of Light wants to speak to you. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.\n\nBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.
94777	Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.	Just a short time ago, one of your priests was here looking for you, <race>. He said that if I were to see you, I should direct you towards the Cathedral of Light. He said it was very important, but I would not be overly concerned if I were you. His demeanor seemed positive... as though it were good news. I wouldn't take too long in making my way there if I were you.\n\nElune be with you, good <race>.
94778	Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.	You're needed in Stormwind, <name>. The High Priestess there, Laurena, says it's time for you to prove you're worthy of the next level of your training. Don't waste too much time finding your way there. You can find her in the Cathedral of Light in the center of the city. Give her my regards, and prove how worthy you are of such a calling. The Light be with you, <name>.
94779	Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.	Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, <name>.\n\nAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.\n\nWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out one of your High Priestesses for further training.
94792	Use the Taming Rod to tame a Rockhide Boar. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.	Many hunters prefer to travel with animal companions. With a beast at your side, you will find that you can survive even the most dangerous of circumstances. As they say, everything is easier with a friend. However, obtaining an animal companion is something that must be done with care. The balance of nature is delicate, and must always be respected.\n\nTake this Taming Rod with you to the forest. With it, you will be able to tame a Rockhide Boar and practice your skills as a hunter.
94793	Speak to Isaac Chan in Goldshire.	You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it. For this, there is none better than Isaac Chan, a lifelong woodsman. He will give you the ability to train your new pet.\n\nGo with the winds, young <class>.
94819	Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.	<name>, your High Priestess Mims would have an audience with you in Ironforge. Make haste, my clever friend, your next test quickly approaches. Although I wish I could bear witness to your race's own special rites, my place is here. But may the Light go with you in your travels. Mims should still be in the Mystic Ward once you reach the city. She will be waiting.
94820	Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.	Your race is so very clever, <name>. We are proud to call you allies. And as each day's sun sets, you and your kin grow closer to reclaiming your city, but with the burden of keeping your families safe in exile. That yearning for home must weigh heavily on you.\n\nWord came from Ironforge just recently. It asked that you return there and speak to High Priestess Mims in the Mystic Ward. I would not keep her waiting. May Elune guide your travels.
94821	Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.	A priest recently visited our halls seeking you out, young <race>. He said that he was on a mission to find you and that you should return to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. When you arrive, seek out High Priestess Mims--she will tell you more.\n\nThe Light be with you, <name>.
94822	Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.	You've caught the attention of our superiors, <name>. They've asked you travel to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Mims. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.
94823	Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.	Elune bless you, good <race>. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.\n\nOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Hall of Mysteries as soon as possible to speak with High Priestess Mims. It seems you've done well to garner such attention. I wouldn't spend too much time here--your people have need of you.
94824	Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.	Time's come for you to head to Stormwind, <Name>. High Priestess Mims in the Hall of Mysteries commands you to come speak with her. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.\n\nBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.
94825	Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.	Just a short time ago, one of your priests was here looking for you, <race>. He said that if I were to see you, I should direct you towards the Hall of Mysteries. He said it was very important, but I would not be overly concerned if I were you. His demeanor seemed positive... as though it were good news. I wouldn't take too long in making my way there if I were you.\n\nElune be with you, good <race>.
94826	Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.	Praise be to Elune, and to your Light, <name>.\n\nAbout this time, many of our order learn abilities reflecting their faith in Elune. If knowledge serves me, I believe the same holds true for your order also.\n\nWhen your business in Darnassus is complete, I would seek out your High Priestess for further training.
94863	Use the Taming Rod to tame a Gray Forest Wolf. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.	You've alraedy mastered taming a boar, now it's time for the next lesson. The forest holds fiercer companions, and with care, you can earn their trust.\n\nTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Gray Forest Wolf. Remember, nature's balance must be respected. Prove your skill as a hunter once more.
94864	Use the Taming Rod to tame a Young Forest Bear. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Josephine Carson.	You've proven yourself by taming a boar and a wolf, now it's time for your final challenge. Elwynn's balance depends on respect and skill. Take this Taming Rod and seek out a Young Forest Bear. Show that you can earn the trust of even the mightiest companion.\n\nCompleting this lesson will deepen your attunement to beasts.
94896	Collect 8 Abandoned Belongings from the ruins of Ban'aethal.	You look like a capable adventurer. Do you happen to be headed towards Shadowgale Forest? Ban'aethal lies deep in the forest; that's where we're all from.\n\n<Ealaane gestures to the other refugees.>\n\nWe've recently had to evacuate Ban'aethal, as it began to fall into the sky. It was sudden and in the middle of the night. If you are headed that way, would you please look for any belongings left behind? The forest and village are far too dangerous for us to return to now.
94897	Find Resaan in the Ruins of Ban'aethal.	If you are traveling to Ban'aethal, I have a selfish request. My love, Resaan... I believe is no longer a part of this world. He had tried to go back to get supplies even though I begged him to stay. It has been over a week already and I fear the worst.\n\nPlease, if you find him bring him home. If he has perished then I beg you to please bring me his heirloom.
94898	Slay 10 Wind Hollows.	When our home started to fall into the sky that fateful night, its as if the elements themselves were waiting to consume us. Wind spirits began appearing as we were fleeing, and to our dismay they began attacking the fleeing survivors.\n\nWe lost many villagers to the sky, but even more to the relentless anger of those wind spirits. I don't know if it was our village falling into the sky, but they are extremely dangerous.\n\nIf you are able, please put them to rest.
94901	Collect $1oa Gustjumper frogs.	[PH] Collect frogs
94902	Collect $1oa grapes.	[PH] Collect grapes from the vineyard
94911	Speak with Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.	Greetings, young <race>. I can see that you have much promise in the druidic arts. There is one who you may want to speak with in the city of Thunder Bluff by the name of Turak Runetotem. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, Moonglade.\n\nYou will be welcomed there, and the druids of the circle will impart their knowledge upon you.\n\nAs your people would say--go with the wind's blessing, young one. I wish you good fortune in your adventures.
94912	Speak with Sheldras Moontree in Stormwind.	Greetings, young <class>.\n\nHave you heard of the Cenarion Circle? I'd expect not. They are an ancient order of naturalists and practitioners of the druidic arts, much like yourself. In the city of Stormwind you'll find a night elf by the name of Sheldras Moontree. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, a place called Moonglade.\n\nGo now. You have much to learn if you wish to save your home.
94913	Use the spell "Teleport: Moonglade" to travel to Moonglade.  When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.	All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade.  Keeper Remulos - Moonglade's guardian - keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.\n\nAs for your first lesson here on Azeroth, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.
94914	Use the spell "Teleport: Moonglade" to travel to Moonglade.  When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.	All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade.  Keeper Remulos - Moonglade's guardian - keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.\n\nAs for your first lesson here on Azeroth, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.
94946	Take the skycutter ship from Zephras Isle to Dalaran City and speak with Danaaris Stargale when you arrive.	I had intended to be the first of us to step foot onto Azeroth, but recent events with the cult have changed my plans. As a result, I will be remaining here in Valanaar for a time. Fret not though, one of our mages will be waiting to receive you upon your arrival in Dalaran. I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we set our affairs in order here. We will call upon you when you are needed.\n\nWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there.
94947	Take the Skyborne Portal to Stormwind and report to Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep.	Its a big world down here, and we need our people to start branching out to explore it. That's where you come in.\n\nThe Kirin Tor is a member of an "Alliance" of like-minded nations. The de-facto heart of this alliance is the city of Stormwind to the south. Elaadrin has asked me to find someone to travel to Stormwind and meet with the regent lord there, a human named Bolvar Fordragon.\n\nWhen you are ready, the Kirin Tor mages have set up a special portal for the High Order to use to access Stormwind.
94978	Use the Taming Rod to tame a Windsong Crawler found near bodies of water.\nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.	Every hunter begins by learning the bond between beast and master. This is your first challenge. In time, you'll tame creatures from every corner of the world, but for now, start with our rivers and lakes on Zephras.\n\nTake this Taming Rod and seek out a Windsong Crawler.\n\nShow that you can earn its trust, and begin your path toward true mastery.
94979	Use the Taming Rod to tame an Ornery Galestrider in the Gustberry Lowlands.\nPractice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.	You've proven you can tame the river's crawler, now it's time to test your skill on open ground. The plains of Zephras echo with the cries of the Galestrider, a proud, winged hunter that runs like the wind.\n\nTake this Taming Rod and seek one out. Travel to the lowlands and earn its trust.\n\nShow you're ready for the trials yet to come.
95034	Speak with Lumina Windsinger in the Sepulcher.	I think you should know that it wasn't actually the Gnolls who attacked us on the road.\n\nWe were actually attacked by a giant, wolf-like creature that I now know as a "worgen". It dispatched our guards and came for me, but Banon threw himself in its path. I managed to get a spell off which startled the creature, causing it to flee, but Banon was already badly bitten. He insisted I leave him there but I refused.\n\nWe were limping back here when the gnolls found us. What came next was terrifying...
95036	Speak with Trevan Rol in the Sepulcher and bring him the materials he requires.	Trevan tells me that the worgen are a major threat to the citizens of Silverpine Forest. Despite their strength and resilience they can be killed, but there is one in particular that just doesn't ever seem to stay dead due to unknown magic.\n\nThat's the one that attacked us. He is known as Old Fire-Eye and he is the biggest and meanest of their kind. To put him down, we'll need a special kind of weapon.\n\nSpeak with Trevan and he will supply you with a list of what is needed to forge such a weapon.
95041	Collect 7 Gnomeregan Archival Data cards from around Gnomeregan, then deliver them to Jemma Quikswitch in Ironforge.	Before we fled Gnomeregan, I made a hard copy of my family's archives. Arcanotechnical field equations, Second War submarine hull designs, Grandma Quikswitch's chili recipe... our greatest accomplishments are in those files.\n\nIt wasn't until we reached Ironforge that I found a hole in my pack! Several punch cards are gone, and without them the data's too scrambled to recover.\n\nThe cards must be buried in the snow, somewhere outside Gnomeregan. Could you find them? I know it's a long shot...
95065	Bring 1 Shiny Bauble and 3 Nightcrawlers to Gilbert Gray at the harbor in Stormwind.	What a view... Best an old man can ask for.\n\nThe fish sure are bitin' now, though I'm down to my last bait. I don't suppose you have any spare fishing supplies on you? Of course not, forgive me. I get so excited at the thought of casting another line it didn't dawn on me I may be one of the few carrying supplies everywhere I go.\n\nWould you be able to help refresh my stock? Catherine Leland has an assortment of fishing goods just west of the Trade District along the canals. Tell her old Gray sent you.
95111	Speak with Ott and ask him to forge your blade.	In Tarren Mill there is a weaponsmith known as Ott. By all accounts he is an unremarkable smith, selling simple blades to travelers. I purchased a sword from him myself, and when I took it to the undercity for maintenance some time later, the smiths there were surprised at its quality. They assumed it came from a well known master smith, but no, it was just Ott.\n\nI'd like to give this orc a chance to do something truly special. Take the materials to Ott in Tarren Mill and offer him the commission.
95125	Watch as Ott forges your blade.	These are some truly fine materials, <class>. You honor me by allowing me to forge this blade for you and I only hope that I can live up to your expectations.\n\nPlease, stand back so that I may begin the forging process.
95126	Bring Ott's Masterwork to Trevan Rol in Silverpine Forest.	Here's the blade. You said that a paladin named Trevan sent you? Please extend my thanks to him for this opportunity when you next see him. Go with honor, friend.
95161	Deliver the Blood-Stained Letter to Avette Fellwood in Duskwood.	If you're looking for Jeremy Heartweaver, your best bet is to talk to his newly adopted mother, Avette Fellwood out in Duskwood. Sweet woman. Likely needs another pair of hands for her work, but it beats staying in the orphanage.\n\nIf you see little Jeremy do be sure to tell him we're all thinking of him, won't you?
95189	Return the Crest of Lordaeron to Lady Dena Kennedy in Stormwind City.	<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in Stormwind would be very keen to get their hands on this.>
95195	Collect 10 Bloodied Insignias and take them to General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind City.	<The old Alliance insignia appears to have belonged to a soldier of Lordaeron. These ruins are likely filled with similar medals that living relatives would be grateful to have returned to them.>
95204	Bring the Crest of Lordaeron to Oran Snakewrithe in Undercity.	<A weathered crest depicting the mark of Lordaeron. With so few relics left after the kingdom's fall, someone in the Undercity would be very keen to get their hands on this.>
95212	Collect 6 Pristine Leopard Pelts and deliver them to Amberstill Ranch.	We're getting ready to send a team of rams to reinforce the Alterac expedition, but we've run out of material to make their saddles.\n\nCollect pelts from the largest, fiercest leopards to the east and bring them to me. It's biting cold up there and our forces deserve nothing but the finest pelts to keep them warm!
95213	Bring the Empty Powder Keg to Quarrymaster Thesten at Gol'Bolar Quarry.	The keg is stamped:\n\nBLASTING POWDER - DANGER - DO NOT HANDLE - DANGER - QUARRYMASTER AUTHORIZATION ONLY - DANGER\n\nYou get a sinking feeling that the troggs shouldn't have this. It would be best to report this to the quarry sooner rather than later.
95214	Recover 16 Stolen Blasting Powder from the troggs east of Gol'Bolar Quarry, then return to Quarrymaster Thesten.	This keg held enough powder to turn King Magni's throne room into an open air courtyard. We've got to get it back from the troggs before they work out how to ignite it.
95216	Collect the Highly Toxic Strain from Witherfang in Ruins of Lordaeron for Theodore Griffs in Undercity.	Welcome to the most vital organ of the Undercity: The Apothecarium! Here we experiment on the most virulent of Azeroth's exotic specimens.\n\nYou've caught me in a good mood, so I will let you in on my latest investigation. It appears there is a particularly venomous arthropod stalking the ruins above our fair city. Its toxins are said to eat through even undead flesh. How exhilarating!\n\nI wish to validate these claims. Should you find yourself withering away from its bite, I should love a sample.
95217	Collect 12 Copper Bars and 4 Toughened Boar Hides and deliver them to Frast Dokner.	So you're looking to learn the blacksmith's trade? Maybe we can help each other.\n\nThe supply shipment's late, and I need materials for some repairs around the camp. If you get me what I need, I'll teach you some of my techniques. Sound fair?
95250	Collect the Head of the Baron in the Ruins of Lordaeron and bring it back to Captain Truman.	What do you want, <race>? Can't you see there is a war to be won?\n\nMy master has already charged into the fray and has ordered me to maintain my post. It has been quite some time, however.\n\nI doubt you'll survive ten minutes in combat, but if it keeps your simple mind busy, why don't you seek out the Grand Marshal. He is the tallest, most statuesque hero you've ever laid eyes on. You'll know him when you see him.
95314	Collect 8 Bottles of Whispering Elixir from Shadowvale, then return to Carolai Anise in Brill.	Before the Scourge invasion, the reclusive village of Shadowvale was known for its Whispering Elixir. Distilled from herbs found only in Tyr's Fall, the elixir was sought by apothecaries, mystics, and poisoners alike even after being banned in the city.\n\nI've had requests from a number of buyers eager to get their hands on some elixir. Travel to the ruins of Shadowvale deep in the Whispering Forest to the west. I'm prepared to offer significant compensation if you can recover some bottles for me.
95328	Deliver Whispering Horror Residue to Father Lankester in the War Quarter of Undercity.	Against your better judgement you scrape up and collect the squirming remains of the beast. Someone in Undercity might have a use for them.
95349	Take the skycutter ship from Zephras Isle to Mulgore and speak with Alana Stormwalker when you arrive.	The recent events with the cult have delayed my plans to travel to Azeroth and I must remain here in Valanaar for a time. You and a handful of other Windshapers will be our vanguard instead. Alaana Stormwalker will be waiting to receive you upon your arrival in Mulgore, and I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we finish our business here. We will join you soon.\n\nWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there. Banu-Alah, <Name>.
95350	Travel to Orgrimmar and speak with Thrall in the Valley of Wisdom.	Its a big world down here, and our new allies are the key to our survival.\n\nThe Earthen Ring is a member of the "Horde", a proud collection of like-minded peoples. The nearby city of Thunder Bluff is a part of the horde, and further to the east lies the capital of Orgrimmar.\n\nSeek out the flight master in the center of Thunder Bluff. They will fly you to Orgrimmar where you will make contact with the horde warchief--Thrall, on behalf of the Windshapers. Winds guide you, <Name>.
95494	Collect 6 Savannah Lion Hides from the Savannah Matriarchs and Savannah Patriarchs in the Barrens.	I need someone with a strong sword arm and some extra time on their hands to help me gather some lion hides. It stings my pride to ask a stranger for this aid, but I took an injury to my leg recently. Until I heal, I'm in no shape to go hunting myself but I have obligations to keep.\n\nThe big ones in this area generally have the best hides, so start with those first.
95495	Bring the Bundle of Hides to the hermit on the ridge overlooking the Dry Hills in the Barrens.	These hides are bound for a tanner who I often trade with. He is something of a hermit and he lives alone on the top of the ridge behind me. Climbing up a steep hillside isn't something I can manage easily right now so I'd be in your debt if you could make this delivery for me.\n\nOh, and about this tanner's... appearance. You need not be alarmed. In spite of his looks, he is no threat. I swear this is true.
95507	Collect 8 Trapped Game from traps found in Sprung Traps in the Barrens.	While you are out there, it would be of great help to me if you could check on my traps for me. I've got them strewn all over the valley.\n\nBring back any small game that I've caught. Keep your eye out for the other wildlife, though. This area can be dangerous if you aren't paying attention.
95508	Help Walton survive the encounter with Terry Longdrink and the Kul Tiras marines.	Yes, I used to be a member of the Kul Tiras navy. After Lord Admiral took Theramore and started his campaign in Durotar, I had... "objections" to his methods. Particularly the methods involving executing civilians.\n\nThere's more to the story but... wait... what's that?\n\nThere's a group of men coming up the ridge!
95621	Travel to the wrecked caravan and learn more about why the Kul Tirans are here.	This morning I spotted a group of humans searching for something in the valley below. I managed to use my rifle's scope for a better look, and it was clear that they were soldiers sporting the livery of Kul Tiras.\n\nIf you'd be willing to take work from me, travel to where these soldiers made camp near the wrecked caravan to the south. Kill any you find and try to learn why they are here.
95774	Slay quilboars and collect 4 of Olgra's Adornments for Mankrik's memorial.	The healer who saved me could not save her, and she has died in battle. Her name is Olgra, and I will never forget her.\n\nYou did not find her adornments on her body? She wore many jewels of polished bone.\n\nSlay the Razormane Raiders near where she fell, and find her precious works of art!\n\nI will place them with the memorial that I build in her memory.
95803	Bring the head of Rudolph Gelhardt to Sylvanas Windrunner in the Undercity.	Now that we've claimed the head of the tarnished commander, I need you to deliver it to the Undercity. Sylvanas Windrunner mistrusts us greatly, and all but openly disparages us.\n\nDeliver Rudolph Gelhardt's head to the Dark Lady. Show her that we tend to our own house and are devoted to the prosperity of the forsaken.
95805	Carry the Smoldering Incense to the shrine of An'she and Mu'sha in the southeastern hills before the incense burns to ash in ten minutes!	The sun and the moon, An'she and Mu'sha, are not part of our world like the elements, yet their light gives us life, guidance, and hope.\n\nWe pay respect to the spirits of the world, and so we pay respect to the twins as well.\n\nIf you would show your respect, take this smoldering incense and bring it to a shrine in the hills to the southeast, overlooking the mesa, south of the quilboar. Be quick, so that you can reach the shrine before the incense burns away.\n\nDon't get it wet!
95816	Bring the completed form to Elaine Compton in Redridge Mountains.	Greetings, accomplished craftsperson!\n\nCompletion of this form will grant you non-exclusive, revocable, and legally limited permission to display advertisement signs for your tradeskill(s) all across Azeroth!\n\nOnce completed, please bring this to your local Azeroth Commerce Authority branch's Contract Coordinator to begin processing.\n\nHappy crafting!
95819	Bring the completed form to Jornah in The Barrens.	Greetings, accomplished craftsperson!\n\nCompletion of this form will grant you non-exclusive, revocable, and legally limited permission to display advertisement signs for your tradeskill(s) all across Azeroth!\n\nOnce completed, please bring this to your local Durotar Supply & Logistics Contract Coordinator to begin processing.\n\nHappy crafting!
95883	Collect a Tortured Soul from the nearby undead in Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest.	<The preparations for a hastily-assembled ritual are gathered unceremoniously on the altar. According to the scrap of note, everything has been gathered. All that's missing are the offering of blood and the Tortured Soul.\n\nThe undead around you look tortured enough. They may have what you seek.>
95884	Find the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest.	<The scrap of note is mostly illegible. What is still readable, however, are notes about preparations for an offering.\n\nAn offering stone is mentioned, as well as a ritual.\n\nPerhaps you can find this offering stone nearby.>
95885	Use the Tortured Soul to give an offering of blood at the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril.	<All that's left now is the offering of blood.\n\nThe note scrap mentioned a 'willing sacrifice.'\n\nAn intense sense of dread washes over you.>
95981	Slay 8 Dalaran Wizards and 8 Dalaran Watchers for Shadow Priest Allister in the Sepulcher.	Taking away their pendants is just the first step. If the Kirin Tor really are shipping a steady supply of relics from Dalaran, we must stop them at the source.\n\nSearch the roads around Ambermill for Dalaran's wizards and watchers. Their presence has allowed free access across our borders for too long. If we can cull their numbers, that should put a stop to these pendants making it into Silverpine Forest in the first place.
95998	Sit near Sam's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.	Well howdy there, <Class>. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. Good for you. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nIt's a big wide world out there and you'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful. Not sure how your outdoorsman skills are but I reckon I could teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire, get comfy. I'll walk you through it.
95999	Deliver the Broken Staff of Incinerator Gar'im to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.	Wanted! Incinerator Gar'im, Leader of an orc incursion in Render's Valley. Purported to be working with the Blackrock of Stonewatch Keep.\n\nBeware of Incinerator Gar'im. He and his Shadowcasters are extremely dangerous. A handsome reward will to be given to any brave soul that can deliver proof of Incinerator Gar'im's demise to Magistrate Solomon.
96031	Speak with Gretta Finespindle in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, <Class>. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.
96044	Speak with Tognus Flintfire in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.
96045	Speak with Vosur Brakthel in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Now that you've taken up Alchemy, I can also teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp once you've learned a bit. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.
96046	Speak with Yarr Hammerstone in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra "oomph" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.
96047	Speak with Thamner Pol in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a <Class>.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.
96050	Speak with Paxton Ganter near Iceflow Lake in Dun Morogh to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.
96055	Speak with Reyna Stonebranch in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.
96056	Speak with Balthus Stoneflayer in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.
96057	Speak with Uthrar Threx in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.
96058	Speak with Bronk Guzzlegear in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.
96059	Speak with Thonys Pillarstone in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Now that you've begun your journey into being an enchanter, I reckon I can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp once you've learned the ropes.\n\nIt's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.
96101	Sit near Raan's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.	Greetings, <Class>. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.
96102	Speak with Snang in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.
96130	Defeat Chakuyak and bring back her pelt.	Among the prairie wolves that hunt the hills nearby is one that is especially aggressive. We have taken to calling her Chakuyak. She has become a threat to travelers coming from abroad.\n\nShe stalks the trees west of Stonebull Lake, moving from tree stand to tree stand.\n\nEnd this threat and bring me her pelt, and I will speak your praises to the chief. Beware, for she is dangerous! You might see other hunters seeking her out there, and perhaps you could work as a team.
96137	Defeat 10 Young Black Ravagers and 7 Black Ravagers then return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire for more information.	A small dagger belonging to the self-appointed ranger, Ira, who kept the forests safe by preventing the beasts within from attacking travelers.\n\nWith Ira's spirit still wandering the woods, perhaps her unfinished business was to clear out the worg that continue to claim victims throughout the forest.
96138	Defeat 8 Splint Fist Warriors and 4 Splint Fist Taskmasters then return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire for more information.	A bow left by the spirit of Merrick Valor, famed Watcher who prided himself on keeping the roads safe from encroaching enemies.\n\nWith Merrick's spirit still wandering the roads, perhaps his unfinished business was to clear out invaders near his home in Raven Hill. The ogres south of town may be what's troubling his spirit.
96139	Search Raven Hill for anything of interest and return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire.	In dark times like these, it's important we remember our heroes as much as our foes. Darkshire would not still be standing if it weren't for the bravery of folk like the good Lady Althea or those who lost their lives at Raven Hill.\n\nHave you read much on Raven Hill? No, of course not. Its history was wiped out along with its people. My library, impressive as it is, has little on the subject.\n\nIf you happen to find anything, I would appreciate bringing it here. Those folk deserve to be remembered.
96204	Accompany Lumina Windsinger and help her escape Fenris Keep.	Now that I'm free I'm going to make these vile creatures regret ever laying eyes on a Windshaper.\n\nLet's get out of here, <class>.
96243	Find Teo Hammerstorm in Dun Morogh.	It's past time ye heeded the earth, brave Shaman. The elements already prickle in yer skin, but once ye speak with the stone, the ground itself'll set firm 'neath yer soles--and in yer soul.\n\nSeek out Teo Hammerstorm, in Coldridge Valley. Ye'll find him within Anvilmar, a holdfast forged by hammer, fire, and will.
96390	Slay 10 Dark Iron Spies in Dun Morogh.	Dark Iron spies have infiltrated Dun Morogh. To what end I canna' not sure, but this is a problem we need to nip in the bud before it is allowed to grow.\n\nHead eastward to Ironband's Compound and kill the Dark Iron spies that you find there.
96391	Deliver the Dark Iron Map to Earthseer Farsen in Dun Morogh.	<The map you are holding seems to show a complex series of underground tunnels and highways that all seem to converge on a point underneath Ironforge itself.\n\nYou can't be sure what the runes say as they are written in the ugly jagged rune language of the Dark Iron dwarves, but you can guess at the purpose of these tunnels. As you are reading the map, a gust of wind washes over you and you can faintly hear a dwarven voice carried on it. Earthseer Farsen needs to see this.>
96392	Speak with Earthseer Farsen's and ask him to lend you his farsight to observe the Dark Iron threat.	Greetings to ye, friend. My name is Earthseer Farsen and I'm visiting Dun Morogh from Aerie Peak. As I was travelin', I couldn't help but notice that we have, well... a bit o' a Dark Iron Dwarf problem.\n\nIf ye have a moment, I can show ye what I mean. I've got a bit o' magic that should do the trick.
96394	Kill 15 Enraged Apparitions, 10 Tormented Souls and put the spirit of Anvilmar to rest.	Something has disturbed the tombs down in the Hall of Thanes, and strange noises have been heard coming from deep within the vaults. The spirits of the dead are light sleepers, and whatever is going on down there seems to have startled them.\n\nHead down there and see what you can do about that for us. If any of the dead are awake--well, put them back down!
96395	Put the spirit of Faldrim Anvilmar to rest in the Hall of Thanes.	The... Thane... my mighty... Thane... he... needs to... rest.\n\nPlease... help him... help him... rest...\n\nConsumed... by... ancient... grudge... No... rest...
96403	Collect 8 Dwarven Heirlooms from the Hall of Thanes.	You there, adventurer... I could really use your aid.\n\nI was sneaking--uh... 'patrolling' in the vaults when a force of Dark Iron dwarves emerged from the depths in mole machines! I don't know what they are here for, but there is priceless loot--uh or, rather... I mean, 'important cultural heirlooms' down there! Please, recover any such relics you see and return them here.\n\nI assure you that anything you recover will be catalogued and returned to its proper place of honor.
96408	Investigate the campsite overlooking the Gol'Bolar Quarry.	Last night one of our mountaineers spotted a campfire on a hillside to the east. It looks to be pretty high up, overlooking  the Gol'Bolar Quarry.\n\nIt's probably nothing, but I'd like you to go check on that camp. If they are friendly, no harm done. If they aren't friendly... well, you know what to do.
96604	Sit near Brakk's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.	Greetings, <class>. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.
96605	Sit near Kaga's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.	Greetings, <class>. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.
96606	Sit near Lyreena's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.	Greetings, <class>. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.
96607	Sit near Eleanor's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.	Greetings, <class>. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.
96608	Sit near Eric's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.	Greetings, hunter. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.
96626	Speak with Tomas in Goldshire to learn to become a cook.	So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, <Class>. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.
96627	Speak to Sam Sarsparilla near Goldshire.	<Name>, you have proven your competence as a protector thus far. That is why I am now entrusting you with an unusual task.\n\nI've heard of a new adventurer down the road by Goldshire. Go and see what he's doing.
96628	Deliver the Supply Bundle to Eric Brighthammer near Kharanos.	Wait, Baz. I have another ask of you, before you brave that tunnel.\n\nMy mountaineers have reported an adventurer that's shown up just outside of Kharanos. Could you deliver these supplies to him?
96629	Speak with Gremlock Pilsnor in Kharanos to learn to become a cook.	So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, <Class>. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.
96630	Bring the journal to Lyreena Duskblade near Dolanaar.	<The journal appears to be quite plain, detailing the life and adventures of someone you've never heard of.\n\nThere are multiple entries mentioning camping. It seems to be quite... fun.>
96634	Speak with Zarrin in Dolanaar to learn to become a cook.	So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, <class>. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.
96638	Speak to Raan Wildwind near Shen'dar Village.	More and more adventurers like yourself have been seeking glory and fortune outside of the safety of Thendal Grove. There's one such adventurer who has made a camp outside of Shen'dar Village, along the road leading southwest out of Thendal Grove.\n\nSeek him out and see what you can learn from him that may help you in your own travels.
96646	Speak with Zerril Softbreeze in Shen'dar Village to learn to become a cook.	So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, <Class>. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.
96652	Bring the journal to Brakk near Razor Hill.	<The journal appears to be quite plain, detailing the life and adventures of someone you've never heard of.\n\nThere are multiple entries mentioning camping. It seems to be quite... fun.>
96655	Speak with Cook Torka in Razor Hill to learn to become a cook.	So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, <class>. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.
96656	Speak to Eleanor Shackleton near Brill.	<name>, you have proven yourself trustworthy in your endeavors against the Scarlet Crusade so far. That is why I am now entrusting you with an unusual task.\n\nI've heard of a new adventurer down the road by Brill. Go and see what she's doing.
96658	Speak with William Pickman in Brill to learn to become a cook.	So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, <class>. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.
96659	Deliver the Supply Bundle to Kaga Wildhoof near Bloodhoof Village.	Wait, <name>. I have another ask of you, before you leave us.\n\nThere is an adventurer by the name of Kaga Wildhoof who has made camp just outside of Bloodhoof Village. She has greatly helped me in the past, and now I see my chance to repay her. Could you deliver these supplies to her?
96661	Speak with Pyall Silentstride in Bloodhoof Village to learn to become a cook.	So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, <class>. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\n\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.
96821	Kill 6 Ridgeshade Creepers and 6 Ridgeshade Lurkers in southern Durotar, then report to Gar'thok in Razor Hill.	We be seein' fewer and fewer travelers from Razor Hill. The scorpids were never much fun, but now I be hearin' there be spiders makin' their nest along the road.\n\nIf your travels be takin' you up north, kill some of the spiders on your way. Then, let Razor Hill know the path's a bit safer for them.
96822	Collect the Raider's Battleaxe, Raider's Bow, and Raider's Shield from the Tiragarde Keep outskirts, then return them to Turroc in Razor Hill.	We lost many brave warriors of the Horde when we sacked Tiragarde Keep. Now that the humans have reinforced the ruins, we cannot collect their remains to properly honor their deaths.\n\nGo to the ruins surrounding the keep, and search for the weapons left by our fallen kin. We will display them in a place of honor.
96825	Cook Torka in Razor Hill wants you to collect 8 Prickly Pear Fruit from the Razormane Grounds west of town.	Our hunters and fishers bring back plenty of savory food for our troops - but it's rare that they get a sweet treat.\n\nI've seen a cactus that produces a prickly, tasty fruit. But it only grows in the hills to the west, where the wretched quilboars make their camps. Make your way past the quilboars and bring me some of those fruits. And be careful - the fruits are as spiny as the quilboars!
96873	Pa'zula in Sen'jin Village wants you to collect 3 Luminous Residue. Luminous Residue can be obtained by disenchanting Hexed Pendants dropped by trolls in the Echo Isles.	The trolls east of here have lost their will to the witchdoctor, Zalazane. He uses many cruel magics to keep hold of his prisoners' minds, but one of his favorite tricks is to make them wear pendants wrapped in evil binding spells.\n\nPractice your enchanting skills by stripping the magic from these pendants, and bring me the results. And don't accidentally put one around your neck, if you value your freedom!
96874	Ug'thok in Orgrimmar wants you to collect 5 Weathered Spines from beasts in Thunder Ridge, along with 5 Rough Grinding Stones.	Have you seen the huge beasts of Thunder Ridge? I keep thinking the spines on their backs would be perfect for crafting the head of a mighty axe. Saru laughed when I told him... but what does he know!?\n\nAs part of your smithing lessons, you can help me out! Bring me some of those spines, along with grinding stones to sharpen them.
96875	Kamari in Orgrimmar wants you to collect 5 Rough Lizard Hide from beasts in Thunder Ridge, along with 2 Cured Light Hides.	Orgrimmar is always expanding, <class>. And when the peons need hides to line the walls and roofs of our new buildings, they come to me!\n\nThe hides of the lizards in Thunder Ridge are typically too thick for armor, but they make excellent building material. Bring me some of their hides, along with a few lighter cured hides. Let's see your skill with leather!
96876	Return the pack to Ukor in southern Durotar.	The pack has the name "Ukor" crudely stitched along the flap.
96877	Deliver Halikor's Hoof to Orgrimmar.	The enormous hoof serves as proof of your victory over the mighty lizard.
96895	Find the Argent Dawn member near the entrance to the Undercity.	Not sure if you heard, but two emissaries of the Argent Dawn just passed through here. I don't mind the Argent Dawn, but I don't like them poking around Tirisfal unsupervised either. They were both Forsaken... but that doesn't make me any less nervous.\n\nOne of them just passed by here, headed southeast. There's a group of scourge cultists snooping around the outskirts of the city in that direction. If those two heard about them, there's no doubt that would have caught their attention.
96896	Observe the conversation between Danitha Morr and Leonid Barthalomew the Revered.	Danitha and I fought against the scourge in the defense of the Undercity when Naxxramas attacked. We lost many good friends that day, including the hero after which this keep was named--Garek Bandarion.\n\nHe might just have been the first Forsaken to rediscover how to wield the light as a paladin. I am encouraged to see his legacy and potential live on here with Danitha and her cohort.\n\nIf only the rest of the forsaken felt the same way...
96897	Kill 8 Dark Neophytes and 8 Dark Enforcers in Tirisfal Glades.	The scourge are a blight on our lands, and their living servants are the worst of them. The people of Tirisfal have enough to deal with between the mindless dead and the Scarlet Crusade. If you wish to do some good, help me put an end to this scum.
96898	Gather 12 Necrotic Crystal Fragments in Tirisfal Glades.	It wasn't long ago that the citadel of Naxxramas bore down upon this city, intent on wiping the Forsaken off the map. Both the Forsaken and the Argent Dawn lost much that day to secure the future of the Forsaken.\n\nDuring the battle, the great necrotic focusing crystal hanging beneath Naxxramas was shattered and its fragments were scattered all over this area. I suspect that is what the cultists are here for. Help me recover the fragments and deprive the scourge of them.
96899	Meet Leonid Barthalomew at Bandarion Keep in Tirisfal Glades.	You've done a great thing for the cause of the Argent Dawn here today, and I thank you. I don't know how familiar you are with the fortress of Bandarion Keep, but my commander and I were headed that way to meet with the paladins that reside there. That was before we learned of the presence of the Cult of the Damned.\n\nIf you'd like to learn more about the Argent Dawn and our mission, seek out my commander at Bandarion Keep, to the northwest of here. I'll remain here to mop up the rest of this mess.
97003	Bring the head of Chol'aruk to Gur'ak in the Barrens.	You there, <class>. I need your aid. There are rumors of a beast that makes its lair deep in a cave at Thorn Hill, northeast of here. The Razormane call it Chol'aruk or "The Ravener". It's supposedly five times the size of a normal quilboar with a thirst for blood that can never be sated.\n\nMost don't believe the tales. But I do--because I've fought its like before.\n\nSeek out its lair and slay Chol'aruk. Bring me its head. I warn you though--prepare well and do not go alone.\n\nBlood and thunder, <class>.
97005	Bring Chol'aruk's Head to Bainham in the Barrens.	There's rumors of a monstrous abomination that makes its lair at a cave to the northwest of here, on the plateau known as Thorn Hill. The Razormane call it Chol'aruk or "The Ravener" and those that have seen it say its so massive that it can swallow an orc whole.\n\nFew believe such tales, but I do... because I've fought one like it myself. On the honor of those I lost to these things, this beast must die.\n\nGather strong allies and find the lair of Chol'aruk. Kill the abomination and bring me it's head.
97220	Bring the Gatehouse Shipment to the stockroom entrance located in Trias' Cheese shop in the Trade District	Every day this week we've been short dockhands.\n\nCare to ease the stress on our cargo schedule?\n\nTake this package to the stockroom entrance of the Gatehouse. You'll find it inside Trias' Cheese shop on the second floor. The mistress, Elaine, will be quite familiar with the deliveries. The Gatehouse often has shipments arriving with more discretion to allow for ceremonial surprises on behalf of the guard's officers.
97222	Carry the Gatehouse Shipment up the stairs in Trias' shop and leave it outside the door.	Yes, it's only a flight of stairs, but if it's such a small ask, it should be no problem for you to finish the delivery yourself!\n\nTrias' Cheese isn't part of the Gatehouse or their stocking inventory, but our buildings share a floor.\n\nPlace the crate outside their stockroom door--the guard will send someone for a regular pickup. They will see the package arrival and carry it inside as they return to post.
97223	Bring Eggs of the Bloodtalon Matriarch to Xar'Ti in Sen'jin Village.	All of the raptors you see before you are ones I have trained myself. They come from all over Kalimdor, but some of the finest come from the Bloodtalon raptors on the isles off our coast.\n\nOne raptor amongst them, the Bloodtalon Matriarch, is particularly savage and has killed many from our village and has become too dangerous to leave at our borders. If you can strike her down, return with her eggs so that we can raise the hatchlings as allies instead of enemies.
97225	Collect 8 Forgotten Loa Idols from the Echo Isles. Bring them to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.	When we fled the isles that Zalazane and his ilk now inhabit, we left behind many precious idols that help us commune with spirits we worship: our loa. They are of grave importance to our tribe.\n\nThe followers of Zalazane show no reverence for our loa and have scattered these idols across the largest of the isles.\n\nThis is an action that will not go unnoticed if we are not able to collect these idols, and offending a loa is a grave matter.\n\nGo, find as many loa idols as you can and return them to me.
97234	Bring the wrapped reading material to the Stormwind library.	Are you here to discuss the deeper meanings of our storied legends? No?\n\nWell, after you're done looking around, can you carry this to the library for me? We're exchanging some of our less popular bodies of work for some more modern writing. I have a list of tomes I'm quite sure the librarian will be able to procure for us within our existing arrangement.\n\nComplimentary club refreshments on us, if you help us out.
97236	Deliver the the Fang of Githyiss to someone interested in the study of spiders in Aldrassil.	A fresh specimen from a beast of this size is quite a find. Perhaps someone in Aldrassil familiar with the study of spiders would be interested in the fang.
97237	Find each of the reading materials located somewhere in the library and then return to Roy Lewells in Stormwind's Park.	I've checked our inventory and all of the selections Mr. Lewells has listed are currently available.\n\nYou will, however, need to procure them off the shelves yourself. Part of our librarian duty is vigilance, and for that, I will resume supervisory bookkeeping.\n\nReturning with the material to Roy on his behalf will not mark yourself accountable for their return; as with his note you're serving as the book club's official courier. Their establishment shall carry that burden.\n\nGood day, <name>.
97242	Take some cuttings from the Cattails and Speargrass growing around the water flows in the Valley of Honor and return to Kor'geld in Yelmak's Alchemy and Potions	Yelmak doesn't want his apprentice breaking anything. Well, anything more than he already has.\n\nHe told me the young mixer in training has too much pride to ask for help when he really needs it. Yelmak wants to give him a taste of a particular home-brewed recipe.\n\nGather a mix of cattail and speargrass cuttings taken from the plants growing around the water in the Valley of Honor. I'd get them myself, but if I left the shop, Whuut would surely know we're catering to his mood.
97243	Bring the Torch of Dormant Flame to Olariaan Swiftburn at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands.	Even though we are in the realm of skywall, this is still the elemental plane. The spirits of all four elements speak to us, if we deign to listen. One among us Windshapers is in particular attunement with the element of fire. A shen'dorei by the name of Olariaan Swiftburn.\n\nBring this to him at the Shrine of Flames in the Gustberry Lowlands. You'll find it tucked away along the edge of the island, west of Valanaar.
97244	Slay Skypriest Faladiel in the Gustberry Lowlands and collect Faladiel's Heart.	There is an Al'Aketh Skypriest called Faladiel. He was once a caller of the flame and a stalwart Windshaper. Like so many Al'Aketh, he mortgaged his loyalty for power and his hands are now stained with the blood of  his former brothers and sisters.\n\nYou will find Skypriest Faladiel at the farm to the northeast past Valanaar, just to the south of the Shrine of Akir. Kill the betrayer. Bring me his heart. It is a gruesome task, but it is needed for the ritual we are to perform.
97245	Find the home of Kuramaa in the Shen'dar Highlands, and defeat the spirit in combat. Bring Kuramaa's Mask to Olariaan Swiftburn in the Gustberry Lowlands when you are victorious.	The residents of the Shen'dar Highlands speak of an ancient forest sprite called Kuramaa. They say it lives inside of a twisted stump at the summit of a hill near the highlands Anchor Pylon.\n\nGo to the highlands and find this stump. Rap your fist upon the bark and Kuramaa will appear. Best the spirit in combat, and bring me its wooden mask.\n\nBe warned however, this entity will be exceptionally resistant to much of your magic. Only the touch of flame will lay low the spirit.
97246	Visit Borstan's Firepit and tell him Thatog wants you to deliver Migi's lunch to him personally.	My son, Migi, always takes off to play with his friends all day. I tell him to pick up a lunch at Borstan's, but I know he almost never does, because he comes home starving. These kids think their games are more important than their own bodies!\n\nPlease, stop at Borstan's Firepit and tell him you're there to deliver Migi's lunch. You can almost certainly find Migi behind Grommash Hold with the rest of his friends.\n\nDuties keep me here during the day and I can't watch over his every meal.
97249	Bring Migi's Lunch to him behind Grommash Hold	Now that I know his parents worry about how much he's actually filling that belly, I've got an idea.\n\nThey made me promise not to pack the same meal every day, so Migi grows a taste for more than one thing. Still, whenever the smoker's full and we're making sweetglazed hog belly sandwiches, he always shows up for lunch. We've started crumbling the leftover crispy glazed bits as a topping--something we can add daily.\n\nTake this to him. Maybe he'll start showing up early and bringing friends!
97250	Slay Alliance soldiers encroaching into the Barrens at the border to Dustwallow Marsh, then return to Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo.	Traveler, have you plans to head toward Dustwallow Marsh? I have heard mutterings that a few human soldiers have taken a stand at its border and are toppling the landmarks left behind by our tauren pathfinders.\n\nRumor has it that a favored tavern has burned to the ground, and in typical Alliance fashion, they immediately cast their blame onto the Horde! I cannot know whether there is any truth to their claim, but their incursion onto OUR land must not stand.\n\nKill first, investigate later!
97253	Collect 5 Handfuls of Complicated Parts from the upper pirate camp south of Ratchet, then return to Wrenix the Wretched in Ratchet.	Hey, got a sec?\n\nSo, apparently, nobody I've sent to deal with the recent pirate problem has come back alive. After five or six attempts I thought, "what if I sent a machine instead?" Turns out, scimitars double as screwdrivers in a pinch, and before I could redirect it home, it was already in pieces and scattered across their camp!\n\nI need those parts back, and since this is a quick little retrieval mission, I'd wager your odds for survival are MUCH higher than the others. Whaddya say?
97257	Wait for Olariaan to begin the ritual at the Brazier of Offering and follow his instructions.\n\nYou must deliver the Eternal Flame to Valanaar before the timer runs out.	Now we will perform the ritual.\n\nI will place the materials onto the altar and call forth the spirits of flame. If the offering is accepted, they will appear and light the Eternal Flame. You will then hold your torch forth and capture the flame.\n\nCarry the lit torch to Valanaar and place it in the Brazier of Eternal Flames. You must do so quickly, for the flames of the Firelands are quick to dissipate here in Skywall.
97263	Deliver Eldrun's misplaced package.	<Several misplaced packages have been left by the mailbox. You note that one of them is marked for delivery from Aerie Peak, to Ironforge, to Eldrun Stormbreaker. It is marked "urgent.">
97275	Give Yelmak's Potion to Whuut.	Whuut is a prodigy. That much is true. But he doesn't yet have the experience, wisdom, and time on the stirring rod to know how to respect alchemical processes.\n\nHe is exhausting all of the rarest and most exotic reagents we have available without pausing to practice and refine his basic skills.\n\nGive him this potion I've brewed with a quick tonic method. He'll reconsider everything he's doing when he learns how local remedies and careful touch are the first true mastery.
97277	Find Grund and Gozwin's camp in the hills to the northwest. Recover Gozwin's Mechanic's Log and kill the Snow Leopard Prowler.	Oi, had me back turned gettin' the boar roast ready when I heard me pal Gozwin screamin' fer his life!\n\nWicked fangs and a blur are all I saw when I turned. Such huge paws! A snow leopard was draggin' its gnomish catch away. I grabbed me shotgun and fired above the beast. It dropped him and sprinted off.\n\nLuckily, it hadn't done more than give ol' Goz some deep scratches.\n\nHead back to camp in the northwestern hills and retrieve Gozwin's Mechanic's Log. Kill that snow leopard too if you see it!
97279	Collect 6 Abandoned Training Weapons, then return to Kzan Thornslash in the Den.	With an influx of new recruits like yourself, it's been hard to keep our weapons supplied. Our weaponsmith, Kzan, is running low on training weapons and I'd like to see what kinds of skills you possess to get an idea of what I have to work with. Luckily for you, I have a solution to both.\n\nWhile you're out there cutting your teeth on boars, salvage six abandoned training weapons. Our failed recruits left them laying on the ground. Once you do, return them to our weaponsmith Kzan behind me in the Den.
97281	Bring the Dull Stormy Orb to Rezlak near Drygulch Ravine.	<Before you is a strange orb and with a dull surface. When picked up a small electrical current seems to vibrate from within. Upon closer inspection, it looks as if a dark mist swirls within and every so often a small electrical spark can be seen.\n\nIt is clear the harpy was using it for some purpose. Perhaps Rezlak would be interested in this object?>
97282	Bring 5 Charged Thunder Lizard Organs to Rezlak near Drygulch Ravine.	"Rezlack, when an opportunity come's knocking make sure you're ready to seize it." That's another gem Gazlowe taught me and that's exactly what I intend to do.\n\nThis orb doesn't seem damaged, it just looks like it's out of juice, but I've the idea to supercharge it back to full strength!\n\nThere are a bunch of thunder lizards in a gorge west of here. They have organs that hold a strong electrical charge that would be perfect for this.\n\nGo harvest some and bring them back to me!
97288	Deliver the Abominable Head to someone within the Undercity.	<As the creature falls, its head comes toppling off. It seems as if it has been reattached several times, and the connection gets weaker with each reconnection.\n\nSomeone in the Undercity would know more about this unique abomination.>
97289	Bring the Head of the Baron to the body of Othmar in the Undercity.	We craft abomination heads all the time, but this one is special. It belonged to a Grand Marshal of the alliance once. A particularly unpleasant one. The Dark Lady had the pleasure of dispatching of this one herself.\n\nOoh the secrets it could tell if it could talk. And it can! If we reattach it to an appropriate host.\n\nGo ahead and place it next to the available body in the next room. But don't attach it. Not yet.
97290	Report your findings to Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity.	You... abomination...\n\nWhy should... help you...\n\nBe gone...
97291	Collect a Toxic Skullcap from Tawny Grisette in the Trade Quarter, Blisterweed near the Herbalism Trainer, and Essence of Agony from the poison vendor in the Rogues' Quarter for Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity.	With the head reattached, all we need now is to bind it to the Dark Lady's will. This should not be a problem. The beast barely has brains left as it is after all the beatings it's taken.\n\nWe simply need to motivate it.\n\nFetch me a Toxic Skullcap from Miss Grisette in the Trade Quarter. Oh, and some Blisterweed from our local herbalist trainers, the Alliestars. Feel free to just take some, they owe me. And lastly a bit of Essence of Agony. Any old poison vendor should do.\n\nWe have a potion to make!
97292	Inject the Hissing Serum into the system above Othmar's body for Master Apothecary Faranell.	I have concocted a lovely serum that our new guest is sure to find quite... stimulating.\n\nTake this. Feed it into the workings dripping from above him. Let's see if we can't show him why it's in his best interest to serve loyally.\n\nAnd try not to drop it. I can't afford a new assistant.
97326	Return 8 Smooth Boulders to Thra behind Grommash Hold.	Hey! You've got time to help us out! I know you do, I can tell by the way you smiled watching the game we're playing.\n\nThis spot behind Grommash Hold is nice because it's clear enough for us to set up our figures. But what stinks is we don't have enough rocks for chairs or tables.\n\nYou're big and strong... d'ya think you could carry back some medium sized rocks, smooth enough to sit on if we need a rest?
97485	Purchase a Bundle of Herbs from Nida the herbalist, a Bundle of Ceder Twigs from Nata the enchanting supplier, and Sinew Thread from Mahu the leatherworking supplier and Ceremonial Flint and Tinder from Naal the cooking supplier.\n\nCombine the items and sprinkle the incense off of Hunter's Rise.	Blessings of An'she, friend.\n\nWe tauren have a tradition of scattering incense to the winds and I was hoping you'd be interested in honoring this tradition.\n\nYou will need to craft the incense by purchasing herbs from Nida, cedar from Nata, sinew thread from Mahu in the mid rise, and ceremonial flint and tinder from Naal on the upper rise. Once you have these items, combine them and spread them off the south facing cliff of Hunter's Rise.\n\nYou will find a mat and incense at the ceremonial site.
97538	Tah Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff wants 30 Mirkweed Pods from Mirkfallon Lake.	Greetings, friend. I wonder if I may ask a favor of you? I have just run out of red pigment for my paints, and I am looking for one with younger hooves to make the long journey into the Stonetalon Mountains on my behalf.\n\nIn the middle of the mountain pass there lies a large circular lake, Mirkfallon Lake, that has a unique plant that grows within its waters. The pods of this plant, mirkweed, turn a vibrant red when dried. Gather the pods of this plant for me, and I will reward you well for your efforts.
97558	Bring Shelene Rhobart 8 Duskbat Wing Membranes, 6 Darkhound Hides and 3 Vile Fin Murloc Skin.	One part of undeath no one mentions is what happens when we are injured. How does the skin of an undead heal itself?\n\nWell, it doesn't.\n\nOurs is a cursed life, <name>. We must take from the living to further our own existence.\n\nWhen we sustain an injury, we must replace our skin which usually means animal hides. Since different hide thicknesses are better for different places on our bodies a variety is key!\n\nBring me wing membranes of a duskbat, hides from a darkhound and skin of a Vile Fin murloc.
97891	Bring the Unstable Potion to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium within the time limit.	You! Quickly, I need you to bring this potion across the slime canal to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium!\n\nIt has a very limited shelf life, and no I can't go myself, my knees rattle and pop out if I attempt to run.\n\nJust another lovely side effect of undeath, apparently.\n\nBut we're wasting time! Here, take this and go!\n\n<Alessandro makes a shooing motion.>
97894	Check on Gorbold Steelhand in Auberdine in Darkshore.\n\nBorgus mentioned a boat on the southern-most dock in Stormwind Harbor that can take you there.	Pleasure to make yer acquaintance! Name's Borgus, of the one and only Steelhand family. You can always count on a Steelhand fer a fair deal!\n\nA few weeks back me brother Gorbold joined up with a merchant stall in Auberdine. Plenty of coin to be made supplyin' ships there, let me tell you! Lucky sod.\n\nI haven't heard from him since--mind checking on him if yer heading that way?\n\nThere's a new ship in the harbor that will take ye straight there. Head to the southern-most dock; can't miss it!
97899	Speak with Whuut in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.
97900	Speak with Dwukk in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.
97901	Speak with Jhag in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.
97902	Speak with Mukdrak in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.
97903	Speak with Rawrk in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a <class>.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.
97904	Speak with Lau'Tiki near Sen'jin Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.
97905	Speak with Jandi in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.
97906	Speak with Karolek in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, <class>. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.
97907	Speak with Krunn in Razor Hill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra "oomph" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.
97908	Speak with Thuwd in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.
97914	Bring Thundris' Letter to Baros Alexston in Stormwind.\n\nThundris mentioned a boat in Auberdine that can take you there.	Auberdine is a humble place, <class>. You will not hear its name spoken in the boughs of Darnassus. Most reference only what the Sundering took from us--the thriving cities of Ameth'Aran, Bashal'Aran, and... Lathar'Lazal.\n\nYet Auberdine remains in their shadow.\n\nI would see our work here recognized. A new vessel connects us to the kingdom of Stormwind, bringing life and supplies to our shores. I beseech you join its next voyage, and bring this letter to a human called Baros Alexston.\n\nMake our home known.
97915	Speak with Alchemist Mallory in Elwynn Forest near Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.
97916	Speak with Smith Argus in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.
97917	Speak with Betty Quin in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.
97918	Speak with Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.
97919	Speak with Michelle Belle in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a <Class>.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.
97920	Speak with Lee Brown near Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.
97921	Speak with Herbalist Pomeroy in Elwynn Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.
97922	Speak with Adele Fielder in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, <class>. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\n\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.
97923	Speak with Gelman Stonehand in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra "oomph" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.
97924	Speak with Helene Peltskinner in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.
97925	Speak with Eldrin in the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.
97926	Bring Alexston's Reply to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine in Darkshore.	I wish it was that easy to help, <class>. I really do.\n\nShould you choose to spend more time in our lands, you will find that many are without. Stormwind's coffers are not what they once were, and what remains is spread thin.\n\nGive this reply to the elder the next time you see him. It's not what he's hoping for, but it's all I have to offer right now.
97927	Speak with Kray in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.
97928	Speak with Thrag Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.
