97971	Speak with Mendalass Tattermend in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.
97972	Speak with Taleen Shimmerthread in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.
97973	Speak with Taleen Shimmerthread in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\n\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.
97977	Collect 4  Gnarlpine Totems and bring them to Tarindrella.	The Gnarlpine furbolg would not turn on their ancient allies so readily. We must learn more of their plight.\n\nSearch their abandoned homes for totems. If any survived the chaos of their departure, their engravings may tell us more of what happened here.\n\nYou'll find their camps along the western edge of the glen, though the grell and grellkin may have scattered them beyond.
97979	Cast Elune's Light and Shadowmeld.	You are born kaldorei--the children of the stars--and have inherited a birthright unlike any other in this world. Elune's grace may illuminate our strengths, helping our strikes hit true, or it may help conceal us just as the moon may eclipse the sun.\n\nOur Long Vigil after the defense of Mount Hyjal has ended, and we have joined an Alliance of others--which you will meet in due time. For now, you are nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil.\n\nDemonstrate Mother Moon's gifts, and bask in her blessings.
98013	Eliminate $1oa Stormscale Myrmidons, 12 Stormscale Sorceresses, and 8 Stormscale Warriors for Arbal at the Grove of the Ancients.	Steel yourself for your time in the ruins, young one... you will not be granted free passage there.\n\nScores of cursed Highborne, now known as naga, roam the once great city. Travel northeast and dispatch them from this land.\n\nWhat they once were... is no more. If they aid the Twilight's Hammer, they can bring only further pain to the forests that once gave them shelter.\n\nWar is what they seek, <class>. War... is what we will bring.
98021	Report To Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill in Westfall.	If you'd like to get started doing some good in our world, I'd recommend reporting to a man named Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall to the south, at the settlement known as Sentinel Hill. His people are in need of aid.\n\nAfter journeying here from another plane of existence, the problems our lands face may seem small. I assure you, the aid you provide to those impacted by such problems means everything to them, and you will grow stronger for your labors.\n\nGood luck out there, adventurer!
98024	Report To Thork at The Crossroads in The Barrens.	After journeying here from the elemental plane, the problems our lands face may seem small. Rest assured, the dangers the horde faces are very real, and you will grow formidable should you survive your service.\n\nIf you'd like to get started doing some good in our world, travel southwest to the vast lands known as the Barrens. There is a settlement there known as the Crossroads. The proud citizens there are ever in need of aid.\n\nGo with honor, adventurer!
98025	Find and slay the owl known as Jai'vhanel and take one of her feathers. The black owl was last seen north of the Ameth'Aran ruins near the mountain base. Report the death of Jai'vhanel to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.	Attention!\n\nA reward is being offered for the death of the owl "Jai'vhanel" also know as "Swordfeather".\n\nUnfortunately this owl has gone mad and has begun to attack travelers as they journey along the road near Auberdine.\n\nJai'vhanel was last seen north of the Ameth'Aran ruins near the mountain base. Bring back one of her jet black feathers as proof of her death.\n\nReward claims for this bounty should be claimed with Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.\n\nThe Auberdine Village Council
98028	Bring the Clouded Water Globe to Onu at the Grove of the Ancients in Darkshore.	All that remains of the powerful elemental is a globe of what seems to be pure water, clouded by some unknown substance. The edges of the sphere seem to be clear until you turn it--as if the cloud actively prevents you from peering within.\n\nWhatever happened to it--and to the ruins it was guarding--is still active in some way.\n\nOnly Onu, the Ancient of Lore at the Grove of the Ancients to the far south, would have a chance at knowing more.
98042	Obtain a Peerless Eye from a Twilight Disciple or Thug at the Master's Glaive in Darkshore and find someone in Auberdine who is willing to take it.	<As you tear away the single page from the Twilight Tome, a foreboding voice floods your mind, uninvited.>\n\nThey have failed.\n\nYou will be forgotten.\n\nThey will lose the eye they gained.
98046	Bring the Drained Vessel to Lariia in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.	<Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm's gaze narrows.>\n\nYou're still here?\n\nTake the phial and get out of my sight, <class>. It is clear my answers do not lie in the waters, just as they did not before.\n\nPerhaps one of the priestesses in the Temple of the Moon to the south will dispose of it.\n\n<Fandral looks away, no longer speaking to you.>\n\nI must look elsewhere if this is to work...
98065	Bring the Moonwell Remnants to Tyrande Whisperwind in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.	You must bring this to Tyrande at once! I will transfer it to a more ceremonial container for you.\n\nDo not be afraid. The High Priestess of Elune is firm, but kind. She protects all who enter Darnassus, and carries our goddess' light to all.\n\nShe will be glad to receive this sacred water. You will find her directly above us.
98067	Place Sentinel Owls at the entrance to the Cenarion Hold depths, the Darnassus Bank, the Craftsman's Terrace Inn, and the City Gate for Sentinel Dalia Sunblade in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.	General Feathermoon ensures all sentinels have time to pray to Elune. A proper huntress wields not blade alone, but gifts of the goddess to overcome our enemies.\n\nYou may help with my daily duties. Place sentinels around the city--start with the tunnels leading beneath Cenarion Hold to the north, the bank at the center of town, the inn in the Craftsman's Terrace to the northeast, and the city gates. The guards can assist you.\n\nSomething is amiss in Teldrassil--we must remain vigilant.
98072	Collect 10 Pristine Crimson Scales and bring them to James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.	You're quite the go-getter! I have just one more favor to ask, if you're up for something a bit more dangerous.\n\nThe crocolisk trade is steady money, but they're small fish compared to what whelp scales will bring. Folks will pay top dollar for a sack of those.\n\nCrocs of the sky, I call 'em! There's no way my apprentice could get them--but it seems right up your alley!\n\nYou'll find whelps far to the east, along the Green Belt. But be careful, there's nasty orcs in those hills!
98093	Sulhasa in southern Barrens wants you to clear out 7 Stormhide lizards and 7 Hecklefang Stalkers in the area so she can leave the tree safely.	I'm so glad you saw me!\n\nThe weather was lovely this morning, so I walked from Camp Taurajo down the golden road. When it came time to head back, I couldn't--a pack of hyenas started circling, and Stormhide lizards blocked my only escape.\n\nScrambling up this tree I went, and now there are too many foes about at this hour for me to make the run home through the fields.\n\nWould you mind clearing out these Stormhide and Hecklefang Stalkers for me?
98094	High Executor Darthalia wants you to deliver updated orders to Deathstalker Masoj, south of Tarren Mill, outside of Dun Garok	Now that we can trust you to deliver critical information to our forward spies, there's an extra task for you.\n\nBring this to Deathstalker Masoj almost directly south of us. He'll have more for you to do once you get there and hand this to him. He is posted on elevated terrain north of the rotten vineyard they call Nethander Stead.\n\nOur plan to take control of these lands continues steadily.
98095	Deathstalker Masoj needs you to place the three Apothecary Vials on peaks around Hillsbrad Foothills and return to him.	Our high command inserts strategic troops using bat riders. Key points around the foothills have lost their signaling beacons.\n\nTake these vials. Uncork them in three locations: the hills bordering Dun Garok, the plataeu overlooking Dunholde Keep, and the last on the ridge of the Headland above the town of Hillsbrad. The vapors that emanate will be like a potent tuning rod to the senses of the bat, drawing them to the desired drop-off points once more.\n\nLook for crushed empty vials and renew our marks.
98189	Bring the Menethil Statuette to Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep.	My goodness, it's--it's beautiful!\n\nThe Blind Princess was to deliver this to Menethil Harbor before tragedy struck. We were so close!\n\nI believe it was to be signed for by Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep just behind us. Why don't you do the honors of finishing the job?
98190	Bring the Menethil Statuette to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep.
98191	Bring the Menethil Statuette to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral of Light.	King Terenas was a good man. A devout man. Beloved by his people, and truly the reason we have this Alliance at all.\n\nThe irony is he was humble--he hated these sorts of memorials, and so precious few exist. And of those, few survived Lordaeron's fall.\n\nIt seems the Light has coalesced in this statuette. It would be best kept in the Cathedral of the Light in Cathdral Square, in the center of the city. Bring it to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker for safekeeping.
98197	Recover 6 Khaz Modan Timber and 30 Khaz Modan Iron from Menethil Harbor for Valstag Ironjaw.	This harbor was first built by the Old Horde as a staging ground for their naval invasion of Hillsbrad. Completely circumvented Lordaeron's defenses!\n\nSo many lives lost...\n\nWhat's worse is that fleet was built with the very resources they stole from Khaz Modan!\n\nPlenty of it remains in the harbor after Admiral Proudmoore routed the brutes and built this place for the Alliance. We'll need it to bolster the town's defenses with the Dragonmaw on the move.
98219	Speak to Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore in Hillsbrad Foothills.	Thank you again for delivering the statuette safely, <name>.\n\nI could use your help with something else. There's a member of the city guard who was reassigned to duty in Southshore out in the Hillsbrad Foothills.\n\nHis father was a friend of mine, and while I don't disagree that he could use the lesson... I'd still like to see him succeed. He would really benefit from someone like you helping him out.\n\nThere is a boat that can take you that way from Menethil Harbor, if you are passing back through.
98240	Bring the Crimson Crate to Howin Kindfeather off the road to the east of Menethil Harbor.	Word is officially out on those whelps, <name>. We already have an order in!\n\nI'll package 'em up all nice for you, then you take it out to the customer. I know, I know; it's just one last favor, I promise!\n\nThese will be for one "Howin Kindfeather". Sent his gryphon into town of all things with a letter for the order! Says he's just off the road to the east, a bit past Whelgar's Excavation Site, if you're familiar.
98247	Deliver the Shipping Label to someone at the Azeroth Commerce Authority trade hub in Redridge Mountains.	<A torn shipping label can be found on the side of the now fully stocked crate. Though the intended recipient is torn off, details of its origin still remain.\n\n"Property of the Azeroth Commerce Authority. Please return empty crates or unfulfilled shipments to our local trade hub at the Three Corners crossroads in Redridge Mountains. Couriers will be compensated for their time and travel."\n\nBeside the text is a crudely drawn map of the area near the aforementioned destination.>
98248	Deliver the Shipping Label to someone at the Durotar Supply and Logistics trade hub near the Crossroads in the Barrens.	<A torn shipping label can be found on the side of the now fully stocked crate. Though the intended recipient is torn off, details of its origin still remain.\n\n"Return damaged shipments or empty crates to the Durotar Supply and Logistics trade outpost, now conveniently located due west of the Crossroads in the Barrens. Your time is valuable and we will compensate you for your efforts!"\n\nBeside the text is a crudely drawn map of the area near the aforementioned destination.>
98251	Kill 6 Shadowhorn Stag and 6 Ashenvale Bear and return to Va'xug Firefure northwest of Fallen Sky Lake.	Gaaah!\n\nI'm so angry. They said Ashenvale was easy to follow. Easy for who? The beasts? The birds?\n\nOne moment I was gathering an herb, the next I'm trapped in this ravine. Do I truly have to circle half the forest to reach where I stood just moments ago?\n\nWhen I'm like this, my spells grow volatile and behave... differently.\n\nCould you thin the wildlife nearby? Even their stupid hooves grate on me. I despise this cursed forest.
98252	Show Va'xug's Eye of Kilrogg the way back to the main Ashenvale road.	Show my Eye of Kilrogg the way out of this ravine and back to the Ashenvale road. Keep it moving and I'll follow once I see a clear path.\n\nI'll stay here--one of us should keep our bearings. If you lose the way, I can guide you back through the eye. I will not have us both wandering blind in this malicious forest.\n\nI can hold the channel for four minutes. No longer. Reach the road before the vision breaks, or return to me and we try again.
98282	Collect an Unruptured Stalker Gland from Thelgen Rock for Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.	Certain alchemical recipes require ingredients sourced from, well, very dangerous places. And those are often just the base herbs! The other ingredients are even worse!\n\nI need to make more antivenom before I can leave again. I swear everything in this marsh is venomous. It's like it runs through the land itself!\n\nCan you help me? I'll need a venom gland from the spiders in Thelgen Rock to the far southeast. But it has to be unruptured, or too much venom will spill out before you can get here. Sorry!
98284	Speak with Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.
98285	Speak with the Strange Hermit in Shadowgale Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	An engineer is ever-resourceful, and if you are in the wilds alone, it's always good to be able to put your trade to use. No good camp is complete without a few helpful constructs!\n\nYes, come back and see me when you've gained a little bit of experience as an engineer and I can show you how to make something special!
98286	Speak with Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.
98287	Speak with Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.	Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.
98298	Bring 6 Worgen Bits to Dalar Dawnweaver in The Sepulcher.	Ah, it's all become so embarrassingly clear! Arugal hardly had any magic at all, let alone enough to create the worgen. 'Arugal's Curse.' Pah! Barely potent enough to last a few seconds.\n\nThese shackles prove he can bind the beasts, not create them. The worgen clearly spread their curse a different way. I would know how.\n\nGo to the Greymane Wall to the south. The worgen seem to be spreading to the humans nearby. Tear the beasts apart and bring me whatever you find. This requires a more direct approach.
98299	Slay 5 Sickly Refugees and 5 Haggard Refugees for Dalar Dawnweaver in The Sepulcher.	If there is one thing we do know, it is that Arugal is responsible for worgen within Silverpine--be it his own machinations or otherwise. What we don't know is how it spreads.\n\nWhile I research a way to stop the curse, our first priority is to contain it. It appears this affliction cannot infect forsaken, but a large group of humans have gathered by the Greymane Wall.\n\nGo to the wall and put down these refugees before they have a chance to become servants for Arugal. And try not to get bit, <race>.
98319	Find Mountaineer Cornelius in the Grizzled Den for Mountaineer Gretchen.	It's bad enough havin' a troll problem, but the mountains are filled tae the brim with wendigos! They normally keep to their own caves, but they seem tae be spreadin' like bunnies. Now they've filled the Grizzled Den north of here.\n\nIf we want Whitebeard's report, we're gonna need to find my partner Cornelius. The blockhead got a little too excited and charged in head first. Brave, but stupid.\n\nHead into the cave and see where he is. And feel free to take out some the beasts while yer at it.
98321	Collect 8 Flintfire Shipments from the Grizzled Den for Tongus Flintfire in Kharanos.	Hoha! Good to see a dwarf who's not afraid to get their hands dirty.\n\nIf yer lookin' fer work, I'm afraid I'm a little short on supplies at the moment. Our most reliable source of ore has been overrun by wendigo and now the cave has been abandoned. The miners had to drop everything when they fled!\n\nSay, why don't ye poke yer head around the Grizzled Den to the west and see if you can find some of our missing shipments. It would save us a great deal o' trouble.
98322	Check in on Mountaineer Gretchen west of Kharanos.	Spelunking dark caves is adventurer business. My job's just to make reports and send them over to Ironforge.\n\nTrouble is, one of my reports hasn't... well, reported back. I asked a few mountaineers to learn more about the wendigo problem we have out here, but I haven't heard from them.\n\nIf you're already going to be out and about, what say you don't check in with Mountaineer Gretchen just west of town. I'm late enough as it is!
98323	Deliver Mountaineer Gretchen's Report back to Senir Whitebeard in Kharanos.	Hopefully ye put down a fair number of the mongrels while you were in there. Shame about Cornelius, though.\n\nFrom what you described, there's not much to report other than the cave is a lost cause. Whitebeard's not gonna like that answer, but I'm not darin' sendin' anybody else into that death trap.\n\nFeel free tae pass along the message, <Name>. I'm not leavin' this spot till the mountain's secure.
98326	Slay Frosthowl and collect the Sack of Fish for Gretta Ganter in Brewnall Village	Do ye know how hard it is to fish on a frozen lake? My poor husband, Paxton, has been out in the middle of it for days and we barely have a single sack to show fer it.\n\nWell, we DID have a sack to show fer it. Until the thrice-damned wendigo attacked me and made off with our haul. It'll take us weeks to fish all that back up! If that loudmouth Frosthowl didn't scare 'em all off, anyway.\n\nDo us a favor and get it back, aye? Drooling brute is hiding somewhere deep in the Grizzled Den to the southeast.
98340	Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.	It would seem that you are ready for the next step in your journey, young druid. Dendrite Starblaze has sent for you, and wishes for you to seek him out in Moonglade once again.\n\nYou have already learned to call upon the magic to take you to Moonglade, so you should be able to embark immediately if you choose. I would suggest you leave soon, if you wish to continue your druidic training.
98341	Seek out the Avatar of Saeyleenan in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the windborne cat.	A spirit of your homeland has recently appeared here and has asked me to guide you to it. This windborne cat spirit has come to tutor and mentor you so that you may take the feline shape of the spirit on Zephras.\n\nAll druids eventually seek this wisdom, though it seems your homeland has a slightly different shape than our traditional one. If you desire to take this spirit's feline form, you will need to undergo our trial.\n\nIt can be found in the southern part of Moonglade, south of the twin bridges.
98342	Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Great Cat Spirit.	To draw upon my spirit, you will need more than a few words. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\n\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics of my favor you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\n\nReturn these relics to me. We will see if you are ready to take my shape.
98362	Return to Thunder Bluff and speak with Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise.	The time has come for us to part ways once again, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to whom that sent you to me. It would seem your instructor, Turak Runetotem, has found a worthy pupil in you. I believe I see one as well. Heed his lessons and you shall soon be able to draw upon the Great Cat Spirit to take its shape.\n\nGo back to whence you came. When the time is right, we will meet again.
98386	Slay 6 Greater Tarantulas and destroy 12 Tarantula Eggs in Alther's Mill for Foreman Oslow in Redridge.	Orcs, gnolls, murlocs. Everything seems to be out to stop me from getting this bridge done on time. Now we have word there's an infestation of tarantulas at our lumber mill!\n\nIf you're up to earn a bit more coin, would you head over to Alther's Mill to the east and clear out their spider problem? Place is as good as useless to me if I can't safely send workers to collect shipments.\n\nOh, and if you see ol' Alther, tell him he owes me for cleaning up his mess.
98387	Bring 10 Battleworn Axes to Marshal Marris in Lakeshire.	What the Blackrock orcs don't understand is that this is a war of attrition. Their brazen push into Alliance territory has left them vulnerable and without supplies, relying on the surrounding mountains to gather resources.\n\nAn army can't run on empty bellies, <name>. Go to their encampments south of Stonewatch Keep to the east and rob them of their food and weapons. Let's see the orcs' fighting spirit when they're starved and defenseless.
98389	Free 6 Webbed Victims in Night's Web Hollow for Aramis Hammerhand in Deathknell.	Greetings, <class>. Yes, I am a paladin. Not even death can stop the Light.\n\nThis my kind have in common with all Forsaken--we have overcome what the living view as their end. However, some even among our own fear us; they suspect we will smite them as some monstrosity.\n\nIn truth, our relationship with undeath is complex, but I am not here to hurt our own. Help me show the others this. Venture to Night's Web Hollow to the northwest and free the freshly raised fools trapped by the spiders there.
98391	Speak to Sister Aquinne in Darnassus.	Blessings to you, <class>. The Sisterhood of Elune has stood as a pillar of kaldorei society for thousands of years.\n\nBefore the Great Sundering, before the War of the Ancients, through the Long Vigil, we have guided and healed our people through the darkness. Such is our charge, and such is the demand of the peerless Mother Moon.\n\nWe now require your aid in a matter of great importance. Sister Aquinne awaits your arrival in Darnassus.
98392	Collect Hatescreech's Amulet, Windmistress Gaedress' Amulet, and Witchmother Arysa's Amulet for Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak in the Oracle Glade.	These belts... look closely at the leather, <name>. Do you see the taint running through the fibers?\n\nI have a suspicion as to its origin, but we will need further proof to be sure.\n\nVenture back out into the harpies' nests to the west and take out their leaders. If their necklaces carry the same darkness as these belts, we'll have our answer.
98393	Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.	It would seem that you are ready for the next step in your journey, young druid. Dendrite Starblaze has sent for you, and wishes for you to seek him out in Moonglade once again.\n\nYou have already learned to call upon the magic to take you to Moonglade, so you should be able to embark immediately if you choose. I would suggest you leave soon, if you wish to continue your druidic training.
98394	Seek out the Great Cat Spirit in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the cat.	In the southern part of Moonglade, on a hill overlooking the bridge, resides a wise and cunning being we call the Great Cat Spirit.\n\nMuch like the Great Bear Spirit, this spirit has served as a tutor and mentor to druids that desire to take the feline shape. All druids eventually seek its wisdom, and if you desire to take the form of a cat, you will as well.\n\nGo meet with the Great Cat Spirit and learn what it will teach you.
98396	Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Great Cat Spirit.	To draw upon my spirit, you will need more than a few words. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\n\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics of my favor you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\n\nReturn these relics to me. We will see if you are ready to take my shape.
98397	Return to Darnassus and speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave.	The time has come for us to part ways once again, young one, as the application of your lessons takes you back to whom that sent you to me. It would seem your instructor, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, has found a worthy pupil in you. I believe I see one as well. Heed his lessons and you shall soon be able to draw upon the Great Cat Spirit to take its shape.\n\nGo back to whence you came. When the time is right, we will meet again.
98398	Find the Oracle Tree Bark nearby to receive its message.	I am impressed by what you have accomplished here in so short a time, <name>. Would that I could ask you to remain here to assist me with my duties... but I know in my heart that greater tasks lie ahead for you.\n\nI have noticed the Oracle Tree has just shed a piece of its bark. No doubt it has a task that it wishes completed. You should speak with it.
98403	Kill 8 Befouled Webwoods and bring Xethorr the Wicked's Mature Fel Moss to Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.	Lord Melenas did not act alone; he was at the behest of another. The one you seek is Xethorr the Wicked. It seems he has twisted the spiders that call Teldrassil home, intending their venom for some foul plan.\n\nHe has taken residence deep in the forest, in the area to the northwest of here known as the Cleft. Take caution, and bring allies, for Xethorr is not an opponent to be trifled with.\n\nDispatch his brood, and bring me anything that may tell us more of the satyr's work here.
98404	Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Avatar of Saeyleenan.	In order to draw upon my spirit, you will need to undergo a trail. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\n\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\n\nReturn these relics to me to pass the druidic trial of these lands.
98405	Seek out the Great Cat Spirit in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the cat.	In the southern part of Moonglade, on a hill overlooking the bridge, resides a wise and cunning being we call the Great Cat Spirit.\n\nMuch like the Great Bear Spirit, this spirit has served as a tutor and mentor to druids that desire to take the feline shape. All druids eventually seek its wisdom, and if you desire to take the form of a cat, you will as well.\n\nGo meet with the Great Cat Spirit and learn what it will teach you.
98407	Collect $1oa Spiked Collars from Gnoll Thrashers for Deputy Feldon near Lakeshire.	If the gnolls are growing so bold they are willing to camp this close to humans, there's no telling how much further they'll go. We need to deter them.\n\nThe beasts are hardly organized, but they seem to respect strength above all else. If we can slay the worst of them, maybe claim some of their trophies, we can remind these gnolls why they should stay in the hills where they belong.\n\nShould you see any of their thrashers, bring me their collars. That should put the fear of the Alliance back into them.
98423	Deliver the Treaty of Understanding to Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge.	Inside of the vault you find a tablet detailing the terms of a peace treaty between the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer dwarf clans. It appears to date back to time period just after of the War of the Three Hammers, and is very likely a notable piece of dwarven history. The king of Ironforge would no doubt be interested in this artifact.
98424	Collect the rest of Supervisor Fizsprocket's pages inside The Venture Co. Mine and bring them to Morin Cloudstalker near Bloodhoof Village.	Some particularly worn papers are held separately, folded in Fizsprocket's inside breast pocket.\n\nThey seem to detail important information that could be used against the Venture Co. and its operations in the region. It would be prudent to look for more before returning to Morin Cloudstalker.
98427	Bring the Clearcutter Key to Morin Cloudstalker outside Bloodhoof Village.	The shredder one of the pages speaks of--I have seen them before in my travels. They can decimate a forest in a fraction of the time that hand and axe can.\n\nEntire glades--homes to the Earth Mother's children for millenia--erased in days.\n\nWe will not allow this to happen in our home, a stone's throw from where our young ones take their first steps.\n\n<name>, I must ask you to gather others, go back into the mine to the northeast, and ensure it fells not a single tree more.
98461	Deliver Hollee's Note to Tarrel Rockweaver near Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.	If you're heading out of Auberdine, I could use your help!\n\nMy dear friend Tarrel and I were classmates in school. Oh, he was such a quickfire on all things excavation! We got split up after graduation--him to Wetlands, and me to here in Darkshore.\n\n<Hollee sighs, then her brow furrows slightly.>\n\nSorry, and his wife... Merrin.\n\nIt doesn't matter. If you go to the Wetlands, could you make sure he's alright? And maybe give him this? He's probably near Menethil Harbor. There's a boat straight there.
98512	Kill 10 Al'Aketh Assassins in the Shen'dar Highlands.	You there, stranger. Get low and keep quiet. We are not alone here.\n\nI was on patrol near the border and noticed that there are a number of Al'Aketh skulking around the house just up the hill there to the north. I don't know what they are doing here, but it can't be good.\n\nIf you want to make yourself useful, get in there and take them out. I'll wait here and watch your back.
98574	Read the Hallowed Memorandum and speak to Branstock Khalder in Anvilmar.	While you were helping me out, this memorandum was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the priest trainer Branstock. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.
98581	Read the Archaic Rune and speak to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.	While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. Based on the Wildhammer style to these inscriptions, I'm guessin' this came from the shaman trainer Teo Hammerstorm. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.
99079	Find Longwalker Malah Longwind east of Bloodhoof Village, near the edge of Mulgore.	The Longwalkers are our people's most trusted scouts. Though their loyalty lies with the High Chieftain alone, young Baine at times seeks their aid.\n\nThis is one such time. Longwalker Malah was dispatched near our borders to the east and did not return last night after three days. When this occurs, it is our duty to confirm their safety.\n\nI must ensure the village remains safe. Prove yourself, and seek Malah out. You will know her by her headband and feathered staff, emblematic of the Longwalkers.
99080	Kill 6 Galak Centaurs, 4 Galak Outrunners, and bring the head of Herak the Pillager to Baine Bloodhoof.	Hear my words well: we will not yield a single blade of grass to the centaur.\n\nGo to their camp now, before they have rested and have a chance to ride to our village. Slaughter them all. Ensure none escape to the Barrens to rally others to their aid.\n\nIf you find the leader of this would-be raiding party, bring me his head so that it may serve as a warning to others who dare tread on our ancestral homeland.
99082	Seek audience with High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.	Your bravery defending your people demands recognition. Journey to Thunder Bluff to the northwest, our mighty city whose shadow grants us shade in the warmer months, and seek audience with my father.\n\nIt was he who led the charge with the young Warchief Thrall to reclaim these plains and drive the centaur away for good. As High Chieftain, he will reward you generously for your part in ensuring his own bravery is honored.\n\nYou must take a lift to reach the High Chieftain, who sits on the central rise.
99127	Check the fishing nets in Crystal Lake.	The fish just ain't biting today, and there's something wrong going on with them. It's not just empty hooks. I haven't seen a single minnow up in the water at all.\n\nLee here set up some traps overnight, go check to see if we've at least got some stock there. If you find anything weird, make sure to show me.
99128	Kill the murlocs at Crystal Lake.	This can only be the work of those murlocs on the other side of the lake. They're disgusting little things, with a vicious temper and teeth to match.\n\nIf we let this continue, there won't be any fish to speak of anywhere in this lake. If you could clear them out a bit, it would help me a ton.
99129	Speak with Remy "Two Times" about Jason's murloc problems.	Remy mentioned murlocs the other day... I'm pretty sure he hates the little buggers as much as I do.\n\nHe might have some ideas on how to keep them away from my fish in the future. I'd like to ask you to go chat with him and see if there's anything he can think of.
99130	Collect ingredients for murloc bait.	I've got a few ideas on how to deal with murlocs. And one of those also helps some others in the process.\n\nThere's a weed often found on farms in the area called duskweed, and in large quantities the petals are toxic to most animals. If we make some murloc bait with the plant, hopefully that can train those creatures to stay away.\n\nAnd some farmers get their fields cleared in the process. Truly a win-win... truly a win-win.
99131	Return to Jason Mathers.	Tell Mathers he can come pick up the bait later today. I'll give him the rundown on the proper usage.\n\nHopefully he'll be able to sell his fish again soon. And we'll have less murlocs in this world.
99143	Collect 6 pieces of shiny junk from the nearby Murloc camp.	Those fish men must think like actual fish, right? Which means anything they like, fish will like!\n\nIf you rummage through some of their junk and return to me with anything that seems like it would make good bait, I'll reward you.
99158	Bring the crate of candles to Father Gavin.	There's a priest out in the mountains that belongs to an organization called the Argent Dawn. They're a holy group that is dedicated to finding and destroying the unholy and unnatural.\n\nFather Gavin though, he's mostly the type that seeks to help and heal everyone rather than grab a weapon. He's fixed up an old building to serve as a rest spot for travelers. I've got a shipment of holy candles that I need to get him. Could you bring them to him if your going that way?
99159	Collect 14 pieces of firewood.	My hearth is open to warm any soul, but I'd like to ask you to help me if you could.\n\nI simply need more firewood. It is something I would normally do myself, but I have been preoccupied by other tasks.
99160	Destroy 10 minor ice elementals.	You may have noticed the elementals nearby. A shelf of rock and ice fell from the mountain peaks a few days ago and riled them up.\n\nThese frozen mountains are already treacherous for the average dwarf or human without the elements taking form. I am not one for fighting anymore--so any of the spirits you can kill would help make the road safer.
99161	Kill Avala and retrieve its core.	I noticed that the first elemental that appeared after the rockslide was larger than its peers. And from what I can tell, it has been the source of occasionally weather changes and other minor slides.\n\nI've been calling it 'Avala', if you could kill it and retrieve the core as proof, I will reward you.
99162	Collect the rifles of fallen mountaineers.	Even mountaineers from Ironforge have to keep their wits about them when traversing through the peaks of Dun Morogh. Falling snow and ice often spells the end of some more novice members' lives.\n\nAfter a slide, I usually try to find any sign of survivors or victims--while praying to the Light that there's nothing to be found. But with the elements acting up, I've held off wandering too far. If you could look for some lost mountaineers and bring me their rifles, I will return them to Ironforge.
]==]

